# a kernel parameter is a device buffer with no binding to rebind, so a whole-tensor `←` into a `mut` tensor parameter of a kernel is rejected; write `target ⇇ source`. On the host the same `←` is the ordinary rebind.

@ kernel
fn fill(mut tf32[2, 2] target, tf32[2, 2] source) → void {
    target ← source
}

main {}
